24. Firebase Security Rules and Backend Authorization

Implement actual Firebase Security Rules and trusted backend authorization.

At minimum:

- Unauthenticated users cannot access protected business records.
- Employees can read only authorized tasks, tickets, comments, notifications, and attachments.
- Employees cannot assign themselves management privileges.
- Employees cannot change their own role, EID, employment status, or supervisor.
- Only authorized HR can edit employee master records.
- Only authorized administrators can change privileged roles and system-wide settings.
- Supervisors can access only records within their approved scope.
- Approval actions require the relevant approval permission.
- Confidential tickets require explicit authorization.
- File access follows the permissions of the related task or ticket.
- Client-side role checks cannot override backend authorization.
- Privileged writes use trusted server-side operations.
- Audit logs cannot be altered by regular employees.
- Deactivated users lose access to protected resources.
- Unauthorized exports and bulk reads are blocked.

Do not use unrestricted rules such as allowing every authenticated user to read or write every document.

Include tests for unauthorized reads, writes, role escalation, direct URL access, and attachment access.

