32. Acceptance Tests

Do not consider the system complete until the following tests pass.

Authentication and security

- A valid employee can log in with the approved Employee ID and initial password.
- First login requires a password change.
- The new password is handled securely.
- Plaintext passwords are never stored in Firestore.
- An invalid or deactivated account cannot access protected pages.
- A regular employee cannot grant themselves administrator permissions.
- Direct API or database requests cannot bypass authorization.

Employee management

- Duplicate EIDs are rejected.
- Missing fields are flagged.
- Ambiguous emails are not assigned without verification.
- Import preview appears before database writes.
- Reimporting an existing verified employee does not silently duplicate or overwrite the record.
- Only authorized HR users can modify employee master data.
- Archived employees remain linked to historical task records.

Tasks

- Authorized users can create and assign tasks.
- Assignment and reassignment history is retained.
- The correct assignee and supervisor receive relevant notifications.
- Employees cannot approve their own work unless explicitly authorized by policy.
- Mandatory subtasks prevent premature parent-task completion.
- Deadline changes are recorded.
- Overdue tasks are calculated from actual deadlines.
- Unauthorized users cannot read restricted tasks.

Tickets

- Authorized employees can create tickets.
- Tickets can be assigned and updated.
- Ticket-to-task conversion retains a traceable relationship.
- Confidential tickets are inaccessible to unauthorized users.
- Resolution and reopening actions are auditable.

Analytics

- Dashboards display actual database data.
- Filters work correctly.
- Completion percentages use valid underlying records.
- Performance metrics can be traced to source tasks.
- AI does not invent completion records or performance results.

Reliability

- Failed writes show a clear error.
- Retrying a safe operation does not create duplicate records.
- Scheduled reminders do not create duplicate notifications.
- File access is checked on the backend.
- The application builds successfully.
- Required configuration and deployment steps are documented.

